    <cas:Sofa xmi:id="1" sofaNum="1" sofaID="_InitialView" mimeType="text" sofaString="During the stormy night, the rattle on the shelf began shaking on its own, tapping out an irregular rhythm like a warning.&#10;Lina’s plush bear slowly lifted its stitched paw, pointing toward the dark hallway where her soft doll sat upright despite having been laid down earlier.&#10;On the floor, her half‑finished puzzle rearranged itself piece by piece, forming an image of eyes staring back at her.&#10;A lonely ball rolled out from under the bed, circling her feet as if urging her to follow.&#10;Outside, the abandoned jump rope slapped against the porch in steady beats, though no wind blew.&#10;The plush bear toppled forward, landing at her toes as its button eyes gleamed unnaturally.&#10;Lina tried to step back, but the puzzle pieces whispered as they slid across the floor, spelling her name.&#10;The doll’s head turned with a tiny creak, smiling a stitched smile far too wide.&#10;Then everything went still—except for the rattle, which shook once more as if saying, “We’ve been waiting.”"/>
